what 80s action star seemingly gets a  loving nod in the new love and thunder  trailer does thor's t-shirt have a  hidden meaning and which celestial  beings return from eternals keep  watching it's hard not to notice the  snazzy shirt thor sports during several  pivotal scenes in the trailer die hard  fans won't be shocked to learn that this  artorial choice may just contain a  deeper meaning which connects it to the  rest of the movie's plot as well as  thor's mythological roots the symbol on  the shirt an artfully drawn tree with  black trunk and black branches with  white circles all the way down placed  against a large red circle is most  likely a visual representation of the  mighty yggdrasil the world tree  norsemythology.org explains that  yggdrasil is a sacred and important part  to the spiritual landscape of the viking  world the tree supports the entire  universe its deep roots extend all the  way to valhalla while its strong gnarled  branches stretch above the clouds  yggdrasil's health is vital to keeping  the living world in harmony and the  cosmos depends upon it when yggdrasil  trembles or withers bad things are  headed asgard's way in the mcu the  original asgard is now just a memory but  as odin said  our scatter is not a place never was  this could be asgard  ascot is where our people stand  so if your sill does fit into the plots  of thor love and thunder the thunder god  may just be the right one to preserve it  eagle-eyed fans will remember that in a  previous thor love and thunder trailer  thor takes the time to meditate under a  tree that looks like idracil the thor  heads to such a sacred spot to attain  some sense of peace and guidance was  interesting enough but his idracial  t-shirt may indicate that enlightenment  is just what he finds there  the last time we saw a celestial  intervening in the mcu it gave cersei a  stern telling off before snatching her  in a selection of other eternals away  from the planet they just saved  you have chosen to sacrifice a celestial  for the people of this planet  now it's been confirmed in the final  trailer for thor love and thunder that  those cosmic colossi are going to make  another appearance just how big a part  do they play in thor's battle against  the god butcher in a frantic escape from  olympus we see the revengers going full  steam ahead and at risk of colliding  with two unnamed celestial beings even  though these celestials to work the goat  boat they still seem small compared to  the newborn celestial that nearly  hatched in eternals with that in mind  the celestials might be peaking their  head not through a window but a portal  of some sort or these are just decidedly  smaller than celestials we've seen in  the past size aside might these mighty  beans be a key factor in defeating gore  or given their antagonistic ways in the  past are they just going to be another  problem  traveling the universe can be a taxing  ordeal for those without an effective  means of traversing incredible distances  in the past the asgardians have used the  rainbow bridge the bifrost to almost  instantly teleport to various locations  this process usually scorches symbols  and runes on the ground this is the  reason why people on earth have a  mythology involving thor odin and loki  because asgardians have visited earth at  varying points in time and their  visitations left marks giving rise to  legends in norse mythology rainbows were  believed to be the physical embodiment  of the bifrost bridge unfortunately the  primary means of harnessing the power of  the bifrost was destroyed during the  events of thor ragnarok luckily though  it seems that thor and his companions  may have found a cool new way to invoke  the bifrost judging by this new trailer  their viking style longship appears to  be generating its very own bifrost while  it soars through the air which may mean  that the asgardians of the galaxy will  still be able to hop around the universe  with ease using a combination of the  boat and thor's goats who also have  origins in norse mythology whether the  boat's abilities are somehow connected  to stormbreaker remains to be seen  thor has wielded both mjolnir and  stormbreaker and can summon lightning on  a whim based on the latest trailer for  love and thunder he's also quite  flexible when two chariots fly at the  word super speed the god of thunder  manages to stop both vessels and their  tracks simultaneously by pulling off a  move often associated with belgian  action star jean-claude van damme thor  does an impressive split with one foot  on each chariot stopping both with  nerius sweat broken the move is  incredibly reminiscent of the splits van  damme would perform in his movies as  well as a 2013 volvo commercial where he  performed the act while on two trucks we  likely won't ever know for certain that  the thor moment draws directly from van  damme's resume but seeing how the  marketing for the movie has incorporated  the 1980s classic sweet child of mine  and the film features plenty of 80s  fashion it seems incredibly likely that  it's meant to be a reference  we've seen thor working with other  heroes in all previous trailers it's  been unclear whether there'll be a full  team up or just a bunch of individual  scenes the newest trailer confirms that  thor if no one else considers himself  the driving force of a very particular  team  i'm putting together the greatest team  ever in a voiceover that spans much of  the trailer thor introduces the latest  version of his revengers or possibly the  asgardians of the galaxy the team  consists of korg valkyrie jane foster  and the guardians of the galaxy which  currently includes star-lord rocket  groot drax nebula and mantis there's  also kraglin who seemingly is a  full-blown guardian by this point or at  least is close to getting there when you  combine all of that power and skill as  well as take into account the many  absurdly powerful villains the various  people in this squad have defeated it's  hard to imagine a villain who'd give  them any further difficulty it's also  kind of unnerving to think just how  dangerous gore the godbutcher must be if  thor has to put together this all-star  squad just to stand a chance check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about the mcu  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

